Feature: The slash-command menu, the door the Compass template picker sits behind

  Recorded live against the GPUI app (sandbox port 8720, SqlOnly / loro=false)
  seeded with a copy of the Compass vault plus the Compass template document
  (`assets/default/Compass.org` copied INTO the vault — the app enumerates
  templates from the block snapshot, so a template file that stays in
  `assets/` is never offered).

  The seven Compass templates DO reach the picker's enumeration: each template
  root carries an uppercase org `:TEMPLATE:` marker, which
  `templates_from_blocks` matches case-insensitively, and all seven are in the
  block snapshot after ingest.

  WHAT THIS SCENARIO PINS. The slash menu opening at all. Live over the MCP
  driver it does NOT: `type_text {"text":"/"}` writes "/" into the block's
  content, no popup appears in `describe_ui` or in a fresh screenshot, and the
  next typed character REPLACES the "/" instead of filtering a menu — content
  went "/" then "goal", never "/goal". So the Compass template picker is
  unreachable through the MCP driver, and every template instantiation in this
  dogfood session had to go through `execute_operation instantiate_template`.
  This scenario replays the same intent headless; the headless transition and
  the live MCP driver disagreeing about whether a menu exists is exactly the
  environment gap worth holding a fixture over.

  WHY THE `Then` IS THIN. There is no step that names a menu entry, so the
  scenario can only assert the menu's EFFECT. The bundled transition selects
  "delete", so a menu that opened and dispatched leaves the block gone from the
  widget; a menu that never opened leaves the text sitting there. The composed
  catalog runs after every step, so a menu that opens and dispatches the wrong
  operation diverges on the next sweep.

  NOT RECORDABLE — picking a named entry. `I trigger the slash command on
  block {block_id}` carries no entry argument; its transition hard-codes
  "delete". Choosing `compass-goal` (or any template) from the menu, and
  supplying its bindings, has no phrasing at all. Reported as a vocabulary gap.

  Scenario: The slash menu opens on a block and dispatches its selection
    When I focus block "block:structural-page" in region "main"
    And I focus the editor of block "block:c2"
    And I trigger the slash command on block "block:c2"
    Then within 10 seconds block "block:c1" is a child of block "block:structural-page"
